User-facing message → Something clean and generic like "failure: Internal Server Error".

Technical details → Logged internally (to console, file, or monitoring system) using a logger.

This way:

End users don’t see sensitive stack traces or database errors.

Developers still have full visibility in logs to debug the root cause.




When you return a Java object from a Spring Boot controller:

Spring uses Jackson to convert it into JSON.

Jackson needs getters to read field values.

Without getters, Jackson won’t know how to serialize your object into JSON.